    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0595" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/485</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Griffith to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consular agent Guantanamo reports burning and sacking Olimpo, Palmarejo and
                    Belona. Yesterday buildings Citero iron mines known Nimanima, Government chart,
                    burned. Government forces fled. <hi rendition="#italic">Machias</hi> left
                    breaking communication with naval station. Captain marines reports two thousand
                    armed rebels near Daiquiri. Mining properties and wharf here inadequately
                    protected, need war vessel and five hundred additional marines immediately. Very
                    urgent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Griffith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
